      "now": {
        "representative": "CadR/PbrR691",
        "inducer": "Cd2+/Pb2+"
      },
      "basis": "The Cd2+ label had NO support beyond the FASTA filename (`..._2_ecCadR.fasta`): this table recorded 'no ground-truth evidence' and mining returned no inducer. The preprint's curation sheet (Table S1_And_Others.xlsx, sheet MerR) assigns cluster 2 exactly one characterized member, PbrR691 (UniProt Q1LKZ5, Cupriavidus metallidurans, Pb(II)), verified present in that FASTA; their logo set also carries cmPbrR_logo.svg.",
      "why_polyspecific": "CadR and PbrR are adjacent clades reading the same chemistry (soft thiophilic divalents via the same C-terminal CX7-8C pair). The filename says CadR, the only curated anchor says PbrR/Pb(II), and neither overrules the other, so the cluster is labelled for both rather than forcing a single ion.",
      "downstream": "Safe: Cd2+ and Pb2+ both map to the same AF3 surrogate ion (ZN) via af3_export.map_effector_to_ion, which now resolves slash labels; and effector.inducer already prefers a query's nearest curated member ion over a lumped cluster label."
    }
